ified goals?interdisciplinary   Interdisciplinary team plan and no plan addressed with pt. Everyone for their own specialty. No acknowledgement of crossover or consideration to work together. When Primary asked is any professional has contacted her for info she could/ would not validate. My primary has been the most involved, however she sent a referral to behavioral service per my chart portal but never discussed it with me. I have no idea ?why? such a referral would be requested! I feel this reflects a poor image of me as a pt and I have never been a behavior problem. At least by her subjective behavior of me . I have always listened been respectful to all involved. Did I question or disagree on occasion? Yes but again respectfully. I feel she felt my anxiety and concerns were minimized to think of me as a frequent caller with questions and concerns. I think but don?t know if was her rationale for seeking a behaviorist.  If so, what she considered a problem I considered a pt right to participate in my plan of care. She would then discuss with me her thoughts. And my concerns aespecially the medications ordered.','Communication between professional participants with each other and then to communicate to the pt the plan of care. I in no way compare my limited education to that of the Medical staff. In a former job I was the PATIENT CARE COORDINATOR. I headed the committee which had authority to mandate dept partipation at each residents update plan of care mtg per NYS required protocol. I would also add after establishing this format it was the first time the state approved the Pt Plans of Care.. I will say this was at a nursing home level of care and recognizing the big difference between nursing home and acute care is substantially different. I only mention interdisciplinary care plans as a suggestion for future thoughts as I feel that?s a big need to include the pt! I can honestly say at this point in my care close to a year. With several specialties involved I d